<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2025" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alternātīo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		alterno, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an interchange</i>, <i>an
			alternation</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: per vices successio, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
			7</span></i> Müll.; <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7,
			5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pedes incertis alternationibus commovere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 10, p. 243, 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., t. t. in the jurists, <i>an alternative</i>, <i>this or that</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 47,
				10, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 4,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 3,
		9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
